### Lot 4 demo, fan side (IntelliJ HTTP client): plan lot-4 §1 demo steps (1)-(8); Lot4FanFlowTest runs the same
### flow in CI.
#
# Start the backend with the dev profile (dev seed: ATLAS FC, admin +212600000001, Ops Dev +212600000003, fan Yassine
# +212600000010 who holds a ticket of a demo event; dev enables the simulated card gateway and cash network and uses
# the log push sender, which prints the path and the token's tail):
#   docker compose up -d && SPRING_PROFILES_ACTIVE=dev ./gradlew bootRun
# OTP codes are printed by the dev log sender ([dev OTP] +2126... -> 123456), or fixed by JOMHOR_DEV_FIXED_OTP:
# paste them into the @...Code variables (the values below are placeholders). Put an ON_SALE event of ATLAS FC in
# @eventId and its price category in @priceId (GET /fan/events/{id}); its sales must close more than 2 h from now
# for a split ("ATLAS FC vs Rapid Oued" does). The other phones are made up: use your own test numbers.

@base = http://localhost:8080/v1
@org = a7a5fc00-0000-4000-8000-000000000001
@fanPhone = +212600000010
@opsPhone = +212600000003
@adminPhone = +212600000001
@buyerPhone = +212611110001
@karimPhone = +212611110002
@saraPhone = +212611110003
@omarPhone = +212611110004
@cashierPhone = +212611110005
@fanCode = 000000
@opsCode = 000000
@adminCode = 000000
@buyerCode = 000000
@karimCode = 000000
@saraCode = 000000
@omarCode = 000000
@cashierCode = 000000
@eventId = 1
@priceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### ---------- (1) Arabic ----------

### 1.1 Buyer (Yazid): ask for a code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{buyerPhone}}"}

### 1.2 Buyer: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{buyerPhone}}", "code": "{{buyerCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("buyerToken", response.body.token); %}

### 1.3 Buyer: the app in Arabic (copy and template locale)
PATCH {{base}}/fan/me
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"locale": "ar"}

### ---------- (2) Split pay: 3 places, his own for "يزيد عقل", Karim and Sara pay their own ----------

### 2.1 Buyer: order 3 places -> 201, total_mad 5000 (his place only), holders[0].label "يزيد ع.", group.members:
### 2 member orders with holder_label and pay_url only (no phone, no full name)
POST {{base}}/fan/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"event_id": {{eventId}}, "channel": "APP", "items": [{"price_category_id": "{{priceId}}", "qty": 3, "holders": [
 {"name": "يزيد عقل"},
 {"name": "Karim Alaoui", "phone": "{{karimPhone}}", "pays": true},
 {"name": "Sara Bennani", "phone": "{{saraPhone}}", "pays": true}]}]}

> {% client.global.set("buyerOrder", response.body.id); %}

### 2.2 Buyer: pay his own place by card. Open redirect_url in a browser and click "Approuver". Each friend then gets
### a SPLIT_INVITE: a WhatsApp log row (split_invite, user id only) and a push (fake) once they have the app.
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{buyerOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CARD"}

### 2.3 Buyer: the group -> status PAID, members RESERVED (1/3)
GET {{base}}/fan/orders/{{buyerOrder}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### 2.4 Karim: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{karimPhone}}"}

### 2.5 Karim: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{karimPhone}}", "code": "{{karimCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("karimToken", response.body.token); %}

### 2.6 Karim: his member order (group_role MEMBER)
GET {{base}}/fan/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}

> {% client.global.set("karimOrder", response.body.orders[0].id); %}

### 2.7 Karim: pay by card as on the shop (channel WEB); approve on the simulated page -> PAID, the ticket is his
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{karimOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CARD", "channel": "WEB"}

### 2.8 Sara: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{saraPhone}}"}

### 2.9 Sara: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{saraPhone}}", "code": "{{saraCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("saraToken", response.body.token); %}

### 2.10 Sara: her member order
GET {{base}}/fan/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

> {% client.global.set("saraOrder", response.body.orders[0].id); %}

### 2.11 Sara: a cash code -> AWAITING_CASH; one PAY_CODE WhatsApp log row (pay_code)
POST {{base}}/fan/orders/{{saraOrder}}/pay
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"method": "CASH_AGENCY"}

> {% client.global.set("payCode", response.body.pay_code); %}

### 2.12 Admin: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}"}

### 2.13 Admin: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{adminPhone}}", "code": "{{adminCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.token); %}

### 2.14 Admin: a cashier (422 TAKEN on a second run: skip it)
POST {{base}}/org/staff
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"name": "Nadia Guichet", "role": "CASHIER", "phone": "{{cashierPhone}}"}

### 2.15 Cashier: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}"}

### 2.16 Cashier: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{cashierPhone}}", "code": "{{cashierCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("cashierToken", response.body.token); %}

### 2.17 Cashier: open the till (201; already open -> 200)
POST {{base}}/org/pos/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"label": "Guichet Nord"}

### 2.18 Cashier: collect Sara's code -> PAID; an ORDER_PAID push is queued for Sara
POST {{base}}/org/pos/codes/{{payCode}}/collect
Authorization: Bearer {{cashierToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"amount_mad": 5000}

### 2.19 Buyer: the group -> members PAID, PAID (3/3), labels only
GET {{base}}/fan/orders/{{buyerOrder}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### ---------- (3) Transfer: Karim -> Omar ----------

### 3.1 Karim: his ticket (VALID, transfer_until = sales close - 30 min)
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}

> {% client.global.set("karimTicket", response.body.tickets[0].id); %}

### 3.2 Karim: transfer to Omar -> 201 {transfer_id, to_label "Omar I.", transferred_at}. Omar gets one
### TICKET_RECEIVED push (once he has the app) and a WhatsApp delivery that goes SENT (log adapter). After the next
### manifest delta the scanner shows Karim's old QR ANNULÉ and Omar's VALIDE. At or after transfer_until: 409
### TRANSFER_CLOSED.
POST {{base}}/fan/tickets/{{karimTicket}}/transfer
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"to_phone": "{{omarPhone}}", "name": "Omar Idrissi"}

### 3.3 Karim: the old ticket is CANCELLED with transferred.to_label, and no k_t
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{karimToken}}

### 3.4 Omar: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{omarPhone}}"}

### 3.5 Omar: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{omarPhone}}", "code": "{{omarCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("omarToken", response.body.token); %}

### 3.6 Omar: the new ticket, VALID, with a new k_t
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{omarToken}}

### ---------- (4) Re-issue: Sara lost her phone ----------

### 4.1 Sara: her ticket
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

> {% client.global.set("saraTicket", response.body.tickets[0].id); %}

### 4.2 Sara: "Téléphone perdu ?" -> 201 {ticket_id}: a new id; her other sessions are signed out; the old QR scans
### ANNULÉ after the next manifest delta
POST {{base}}/fan/tickets/{{saraTicket}}/reissue
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

### 4.3 Sara: only the new ticket is listed
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{saraToken}}

### ---------- (5) Matchday ----------

### 5.1 Buyer: the gate side of his ticket (gates with directions and coordinates)
GET {{base}}/fan/tickets?with_keys=true
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### 5.2 Buyer: gate load chips and his entries. Scan his QR with a Lot 2 scanner (lot2-gate.http): once the scan
### syncs, entries holds his ticket ("Tu es dedans"). Omar sees only his own; a fan with no ticket gets 404.
GET {{base}}/fan/gates/{{eventId}}/load
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### ---------- (6) Membership ----------

### 6.1 Buyer: join ATLAS FC with push on -> 201, member.number
PUT {{base}}/fan/me/membership
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"organizer_id": "{{org}}", "marketing_push": true, "marketing_whatsapp": false}

### 6.2 Omar: join with push off
PUT {{base}}/fan/me/membership
Authorization: Bearer {{omarToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"organizer_id": "{{org}}", "marketing_push": false, "marketing_whatsapp": false}

### 6.3 Buyer: after the event closes (lot2-gate.http step 5) -> loyalty.events_attended 1 and the event attended
### in last_events (Omar's too: the transferred ticket counts for him)
GET {{base}}/fan/me/membership?organizer={{org}}
Authorization: Bearer {{buyerToken}}

### ---------- (7) Campaigns: the BE-33 section below (C1-C14) ----------

### ---------- (8) Back-office ----------

### 8.1 B3: paid 3 for the split, unchanged by the transfer and the re-issue
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/sales
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 8.2 B4: sold, unchanged likewise
GET {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/live
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### 8.3 B12: the transfer chain from Omar's phone (transferred_from = Karim's ticket number)
POST {{base}}/org/events/{{eventId}}/tickets/search
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"q": "{{omarPhone}}"}

### 8.4 B9: member counts (counts only)
GET {{base}}/org/members/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### ---------- Campaigns and the inbox (BE-33) ----------

### C1. Fan: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{fanPhone}}"}

### C2. Fan: verify
POST {{base}}/fan/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{fanPhone}}", "code": "{{fanCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("fanToken", response.body.token); %}

### C3. Fan: a fake push token for this session (the log sender accepts any token) -> 204
PUT {{base}}/fan/me/push-token
Authorization: Bearer {{fanToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"token": "dev-fake-{{$random.uuid}}", "platform": "android"}

### C4. Fan: join ATLAS FC with the push opt-in on -> 201 (200 if already a member)
PUT {{base}}/fan/me/membership
Authorization: Bearer {{fanToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"organizer_id": "{{org}}", "marketing_push": true, "marketing_whatsapp": false}

### C5. Ops: ask for a code
POST {{base}}/org/auth/otp
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}"}

### C6. Ops: verify
POST {{base}}/org/auth/verify
Content-Type: application/json

{"phone": "{{opsPhone}}", "code": "{{opsCode}}"}

> {% client.global.set("opsToken", response.body.token); %}

### C7. Ops: the members summary (counts only)
GET {{base}}/org/members/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### C8. Ops: a PUSH MEMBERS campaign opening the event -> 201 DRAFT, audience_estimate >= 1
POST {{base}}/org/campaigns
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"channel": "PUSH", "audience": "MEMBERS", "event_id": {{eventId}}, "title": "Derby samedi",
 "body": "Les billets partent vite : réserve ta place dans l'app."}

> {% client.global.set("pushCampaign", response.body.id); %}

### C9. Ops: send now (no body) -> SCHEDULED. Wait about 35 s: the job snapshots it, the outbox sends it.
POST {{base}}/org/campaigns/{{pushCampaign}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### C10. Ops: the list -> SENT, recipients 1, sent 1
GET {{base}}/org/campaigns
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}

### C11. Fan: the inbox -> the campaign with the ATLAS FC organizer block
GET {{base}}/fan/me/inbox
Authorization: Bearer {{fanToken}}

### C12. Ops: a WhatsApp EVENT_HOLDERS campaign (service info: every VALID holder of the event)
POST {{base}}/org/campaigns
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"channel": "WHATSAPP", "audience": "EVENT_HOLDERS", "event_id": {{eventId}}, "title": "Ouverture des portes",
 "body": "Ouverture des portes à 18 h"}

> {% client.global.set("holdersCampaign", response.body.id); %}

### C13. Ops: send it now; after about 35 s GET it: SENT, one row per VALID holder (the log adapter prints user ids)
POST {{base}}/org/campaigns/{{holdersCampaign}}/send
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}

### C14. Ops: the campaign
GET {{base}}/org/campaigns/{{holdersCampaign}}
Authorization: Bearer {{opsToken}}
X-Organizer-Id: {{org}}
